\title{RSCopying: Protocol for Object Copying}
\description{
\code{RSCopying} is a protocol that defines a contract for objects that can be copied
into another environment. Conforming objects must implement the method
\code{copyWithEnv(env)}, which produces a deep copy of the object into the specified environment.

This protocol is typically used when copying values between container objects
(e.g., \code{RSSet}, \code{RSDictionary}) or when isolating mutable scope.
}
\section{Required Method}{

\itemize{
\item \code{copyWithEnv(env)} — Returns a copy of the object placed into a specified environment.
}
}

\section{Helper}{

\itemize{
\item \code{copyObjectWithEnv(copying_obj, env)} — Calls \code{copyWithEnv()} on a conforming object.
}
}

